{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1510895-have-you-ever-ignored-the-7-points-of-flaws-limit","id":1510895,"title":"Have you ever ignored the 7 points of flaws limit?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-06T11:18:42-07:00","id":1510895,"title":"Have you ever ignored the 7 points of flaws limit?","content":"Do you go RAW, tweak it a bit or ignore it?<br /> I tend to say you can take every flaw in the book if you like, but you'll only get 7 extra freebie points out of it. Although the temptation to just get, like, 100 freebie points by continuing to add flaws until I have all the dots I need-want is strong; I would create the most skilled and the single most cursed person on the planet. Juggling an infinite amount of flaws and merits is a headache though, so the limit is perfectly understandable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T12:28:42-07:00","id":1510906,"title":"","content":"Essentially the same: you can be as flawed as you like, but you're only getting seven points. <br /> <br /> there might be some leway in that if someone wants to make merits cheaper by adding downsides to them I might not consider that an addition to the flaw limit. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T14:26:31-07:00","id":1510917,"title":"","content":"I've done the &quot;max 7 freebies, but if you want more Flaws go for it,&quot; enough times that it's basically a standard house rule in my games unless I'm dealing with mostly fresh WoD players.<br /> <br /> Something else I do, is something I call &quot;packaging&quot; Backgrounds, Merits and Flaws; and only the net value counts towards limits. So if you have a Merit and a Flaw that are just inexplicably linked such that losing one without losing the other is narratively impossible, they count as one &quot;trait&quot; and if the net value is negative that goes to your 7 point limit, not the base value of the Flaw. Yes, this does allow for a bit more oomph for characters, but because they have to be packaged to count the benefit to the story has always been better than any headaches from characters having a bit more power and pitfalls at start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T17:05:14-07:00","id":1510929,"title":"","content":"In my experience, Flaws work best when players actually want them as a roleplay tool. Whatever Flaw it is, for those players it's part of their concept for their character. They want to roleplay the Flaw. The extra build points are just a bonus. As a result, they rarely need seven points of Flaws, much less more.<br /> <br /> Flaws don't work when players use them simply as a means to generate more build points. Those players don't want to roleplay the Flaws and hope to ignore them as much as possible. Instead of a solid character, you get this strange hodge podge of defects. If the ST pushes the player into roleplaying their Flaws, their PC quickly becomes a character nobody wants in the game. Unfortunately, most players fall under this category.<br /> <br /> If the players really want to start play with more powerful vampires, it is probably just best for the group to ask the ST if they can have more Freebies or XP at character creation.<br /> <br /> Merits and Flaws work best as rare elements to spice up a character and highlight something the player wants as part of their core characteristics IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-06T17:31:33-07:00","id":1510935,"title":"","content":"While I like other design approaches than how the WoD works, I think it's worth remembering in a thread that's not game specific, that different games within the WoD can have wildly different lists, which can lead to wildly different player reactions. Mage, for example, works way better with a more liberal approach to Merits and Flaws because they're really good for adding lots of flavor to characters because Mage's core mechanics are more universal. Mage is absolutely the game where I've seen the most cases of players requesting more than 7 points worth of Flaws, even if they don't get more bonus points out of it. Changeling is a close second place.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's as simple as &quot;Merits and Flaws are best if rare.&quot; because different games benefit from what you can do with them in different ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T02:09:39-07:00","id":1510965,"title":"","content":"I used to, but only if I really liked the concept that tied it all together. For example, getting all of the classic Hammer Dracula weaknesses(silver, invitations, etc) took more than seven, but I allowed it because I liked the concept of going full Dracula.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T03:55:55-07:00","id":1511600,"title":"","content":"I have a definite taste for OP and complex character concepts, so I ignore that rule (and similar ones) all the time. I make an effort to justify everything I use in a coherent concept, but that rule might well be non-existent for me. To get a sample of what I deal with, look at <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1477034-demonic-investment-flaws-for-op-nephilim\">this</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T15:21:12-07:00","id":1511742,"title":"","content":"Honestly the way WoD sets up it's flaws is just terrible and a remnant of the original designers working from more of a wargame philosophy. It's also honestly quite insulting, but this isn't really a thread about the philosophy of flaw purchasing systems. But the best games are the ones that make you excited to take a flaw, where the fact that your character has one arm is more important than the fact that they have eidetic memory. In WoD flaws are something to be grabbed in character creation and then minimised in actual play <br /> <br /> Honestly, I always just assumed that after taking all your flaws you totalled their values and took the lower of the result or seven. It makes sense, it minimise taking a bucket of flaws for the points, but it doesn't cause the issue of 'I want X and Y, but they're both four points so I have to pick one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T00:58:30-07:00","id":1511775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1510895-have-you-ever-ignored-the-7-points-of-flaws-limit?p=1511742#post1511742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In WoD flaws are something to be grabbed in character creation and then minimised in actual play</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? In my experience at my table we love flaws for the roleplay reasons - more than merits - it's why I ruled that you can take more than seven points worth (sans gaining more than seven points). Obviously you can just say &quot;my character lost an eye before embrace&quot; or something, but it's nice to have the flaws to have mechanics and a list to keep tabs on for the reminder. Although I suppose it's not surprising that they would also just be used as a way to get more freebies to spend while minimising the actual impact they would have on play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-16T02:30:30-07:00","id":1511782,"title":"","content":"Indeed<br /> Flaws are loaded guns you gave to your ST to shoot you in the head<br /> And they are awesome... my players *know* I will torment them and spin stories around their Flaws and weaknesess, backstory tidbits and so on (heck, even disciplines; okay Potance give you might... but if you don't take up Fortitude? The might to break solid granite wall is nice, but you would ends up with a borken arm... in the line of the classic:<br /> <br /> 6yo DM: With your Ring of Jumping you soar 20' into the air but just miss the ladder.<br /> Me: I will try something else.<br /> 6yo DM: You take 9 points of falling damage.<br /> Me: I am wearing the Ring of Jumping!!!<br /> 6yo DM: It isn't the Ring of <i>Landing.</i><br /> <br /> I always allows them to take as many as they like to make their dream character (most of the time they don't even use up the point, just take them)<br /> Never had the misfortune to have a ST or players who minimised these things","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T10:56:11-07:00","id":1511887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1510895-have-you-ever-ignored-the-7-points-of-flaws-limit#post1510895\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you go RAW, tweak it a bit or ignore it?<br /> I tend to say you can take every flaw in the book if you like, but you'll only get 7 extra freebie points out of it. Although the temptation to just get, like, 100 freebie points by continuing to add flaws until I have all the dots I need-want is strong; I would create the most skilled and the single most cursed person on the planet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that flaws ( or disadvantages, or imperfections ) definitely do not have to result in a weakness, a failing, or a limitation. There might be many situations for a protagonist / character where a seemingly negative or problematic circumstance / quality would not cause any trouble - in fact it might even turn a situation around positively.<br /> <br /> Comparably, I think that merits ( or advantages or distinctions ) might come with drawbacks, and their good and positive qualities and effects might not be active or relevant in some situations or events.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 06-02-2023, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T14:27:56-07:00","id":1511916,"title":"","content":"While it can be a fun narrative, keep in mind it can feel very off-putting to people with disabilities when games portray disabilities as, well, not disabling. It doesn't mean you have to copy real world impairments, but if disabilities give you a boost somewhere else (mechanically or narratively) - including being part of the price of an advantageous trait - it feels like you're not really thinking about how these things can very drastically negatively impact people's lives. <br /> <br /> People with hearing impairments don't just get the ability to read lips or learn sign language as a perk. Those are skills they had to learn on top of all the other skills they have to learn to cope in a world designed around people that hear within normal human average. It's less time and energy to put into other things, not more. Also, anyone can learn to sign or read lips. Having the deaf character miraculously always happen to be the one that eavesdrop on a conversation covertly because they don't need to hear it, or communicate near silently, is both a stretch and trying to hard to turn a hardship into a positive.<br /> <br /> There isn't necessarily a right or good answer to this issue. But if you're thinking about how to approach thing like Merits and Flaws, it's worth considering how someone with those traits would feel about how your house rules/etc. would react to your implementation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T14:05:30-07:00","id":1512486,"title":"","content":"There is a flaw, from Mage - Revised that seems to allow exceeding the 7 point limit<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Aging</b><br /> <br /> <br /> (5 points) [Mage: Revised - Physical Flaw]<br /> <br /> Your mage is either not as spry as he used to be, or he is not yet mature. Either way, one Physical Attribute score (your choice) must be lowered by one point. This Flaw must be taken once per decade over the 40-year mark, or once for each age bracket under 15. Your character loses one dot between the ages of 11 and 14, two for being between seven and 10, and he loses three for being between four and six. If you take this Flaw to represent youth, you must also take the Child Flaw.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div><br /> It talks about taking the flaws two or three time, but that would mean 10 or 15 points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8595,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","user":"Conradine","date":". 05-23-2023, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T20:42:58-07:00","id":1512816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1510895-have-you-ever-ignored-the-7-points-of-flaws-limit?p=1510929#post1510929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my experience, Flaws work best when players actually want them as a roleplay tool. . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the best response. There as to be a reason the players are getting flaws and mostly, it's only because they want more points. Like Dark Fate: really? They're a vampire; how much darker are things going to get?<br /> <br /> Once, for a vamp-game, I made all my players start out as mortals and we'd role-play their embrace, but, it turned out, the players were happy just playing mortals, which, I was rather surprised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T04:45:16-07:00","id":1514569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1510895-have-you-ever-ignored-the-7-points-of-flaws-limit?p=1510935#post1510935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I like other design approaches than how the WoD works, I think it's worth remembering in a thread that's not game specific, that different games within the WoD can have wildly different lists, which can lead to wildly different player reactions. <b>Mage, for example, works way better with a more liberal approach to Merits and Flaws because they're really good for adding lots of flavor to characters because Mage's core mechanics are more universal. Mage is absolutely the game where I've seen the most cases of players requesting more than 7 points worth of Flaws, even if they don't get more bonus points out of it. Changeling is a close second place.</b><br /> <br /> I don't think it's as simple as &quot;Merits and Flaws are best if rare.&quot; because different games benefit from what you can do with them in different ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, M20 has an optional rule to start with up to 13 points of flaws (and their corresponding freebies).<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26836_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26836\" data-vbnamecard=\"26836\">Rhywbeth</a> Remember that this game is about roleplaying, you can go for the most redundant or least damaging flaws for your character for min-maxing, but the idea is that flaws will give you material to make your character more nuanced and give the Storyteller something to work to provide you with interesting plots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T05:34:17-07:00","id":1514571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1510895-have-you-ever-ignored-the-7-points-of-flaws-limit?p=1514569#post1514569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26836_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26836\" data-vbnamecard=\"26836\">Rhywbeth</a> Remember that this game is about roleplaying, you can go for the most redundant or least damaging flaws for your character for min-maxing, but the idea is that flaws will give you material to make your character more nuanced and give the Storyteller something to work to provide you with interesting plots.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know?<br /> If it's about the infinite freebies thing, that was meant as a joke; <i>&quot;the most skilled and the single most cursed person on the planet&quot;</i> is not a serious character concept meant for playing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 06-11-2023, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-15T18:47:32-07:00","id":1515196,"title":"","content":"And to answer the question, more clearly, no. Before WoD &amp; V:tM, we played Cyberpunk:2020 and one player would sell their soul, three times (to the Mafia, Military and Corporations), to get a total of 30,000 euro-bucks to spend on Cyberware. And when playing V:tM, that very same player would use freebies as points, not freebies; I mean, if you're gonna cheat, at least be subtle about it so we don't look at your character sheet and think your neonate is an elder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T13:03:03-07:00","id":1515552,"title":"","content":"I used to play in a group in which the storyteller allowed 14 points worth of flaws. And it got pretty ridiculous. There were some old school rules lawyers in the party.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}